        <div id="handheld-vs-backpack" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Handheld vs Backpack Gas Leaf Blowers: Which Do You Need?
          </h2>

          <p>
            The best gas leaf blower depends mostly on your yard's size. Handheld and backpack blowers do the same job at very different scales.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Handheld Gas Blowers</h3>

          <p>
            Handhelds, like the Husqvarna 125BVx and ECHO PB-2520, weigh around 10 to 12 pounds and suit driveways, patios and lawns up to about half an acre. Many convert to vacuums for beds and corners.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Backpack Gas Blowers</h3>

          <p>
            Backpacks, like the Husqvarna 150BT and Poulan Pro PR48BT, carry a bigger engine on a harness. Poulan Pro aims the PR48BT at yards of half an acre and up, and they handle wet leaves far better. Our <a href="/best-backpack-leaf-blower/">backpack leaf blower guide</a> covers pro models.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">A Rule of Thumb</h3>

          <p>
            Under half an acre with mostly dry leaves, a handheld is enough. Over half an acre, many trees or wet leaves, a backpack saves hours and your arm.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="cfm-mph" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. CFM vs MPH: What the Numbers Mean
          </h2>

          <p>
            Every blower lists two numbers, and they measure different things.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">CFM Moves Volume</h3>

          <p>
            Cubic feet per minute is how much air the blower moves. Higher CFM moves bigger piles of leaves across the lawn. The picks here range from 391 CFM (ECHO ES-250) to 765 CFM (Husqvarna 150BT).
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">MPH Lifts Stuck Debris</h3>

          <p>
            Air speed in MPH loosens leaves stuck to the ground and blows debris out of cracks. High MPH with low CFM gives a narrow, fast jet that moves little volume.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Newtons Combine Both</h3>

          <p>
            Some makers, like Husqvarna, list blowing force in newtons (12.5 N for the 125BVx, 22 N for the 150BT), which reflects both volume and speed and is the most useful single figure.
          </p>

